WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.780
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:07.710
I have the flu and everything hurts, and I am miserable and the world is a smoking pile of burnt garbage, and today

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:11.480
I would like to try to cheer myself up, by telling you two love stories.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:15.178
Okay, so back in January of 2012 when my book The Fault in Our Stars came out,

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:20.960
we went on tour for about a month, and one of our first stops was this hotel ballroom, outside of Washington DC.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.860
Before that show, a bunch of nerdfighters met up to hang out, two of whom were Sara and Luis.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:29.371
Now, they'd never met each other before, but they really hit it off on this day,

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.280
and so they exchanged contact information, and then eventually they began dating.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:38.414
They fell in love, acquired a dog named Scout and a cat named Boo, and then decided to get married.

00:00:38.414 --> 00:00:41.489
And they accomplished all of this while I was failing to write a new book.

00:00:41.489 --> 00:00:43.379
But then I did write a new book.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.840
And we announced that we were going on tour, and returning to Washington DC,

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.900
on a day that just happened to be two days before Luis and Sara's wedding.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.020
And even though it was, of course, a very busy time for them, they managed to make it to the Turtles All the Way Down tour,

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.300
where we presented them with a KitchenAid mixer and a bottle of champagne.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:01.340
Because, you know, that's what you need in a new marriage:

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:04.600
love, a KitchenAid mixer, and something bubbly to celebrate with.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:08.080
And then they got married! With lots of nerdfighter friends in attendance.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.840
The wedding's dress code was, and I'm quoting directly here, 'comfortable but dressy rainbow colors.'

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.466
Which means it was almost certainly the greatest wedding ever.

00:01:15.466 --> 00:01:17.033
And also, look at these nerdfighters!

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:20.720
Look at all of these wonderful people celebrating joy and love!

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.860
Behold hope and life and everything that is not influenza!

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:29.840
I just barfed between takes, so that's how my day's going. Let's go on to the second love story.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:34.400
Okay, we're going back to 2012. So that October, I visited a library in Cincinnati.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:39.360
And a couple days before the event, a guy named Kenny tweeted me to ask if he should skip his business law class to

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:44.240
come to my book reading, and I said no, because you know, school is more important, but he came anyway.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.620
And he happened to sit next to someone named Amy.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.560
They chatted before and after the show, exchanged contact information,

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:53.640
and then eventually fell in love! They got two dogs and three cats and bought a house together,

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:59.520
and then a couple days before our return to Cincinnati for the Turtles All the Way Down tour, Kenny wrote to me on Reddit.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.909
He said, "I met my girlfriend five years ago at your book signing in Cincinnati.

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:05.660
I want to propose now, but don't know how. Any advice?"

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:19.760
Congratulations, Kenny and Amy! Here's a couple pieces of unsolicited wedding advice.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.720
One: Nothing matters except whether you have an open bar, and

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:27.140
two: If at all possible, make your dress code comfortable, but dressy rainbow colors.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.980
Now I know what the vast majority of you are thinking:

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.770
"Why hasn't this ever happened to me?" And fair enough.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:37.520
But you have to remember, if you're lucky, this happens to you exactly once in your life.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:42.440
Hank, we are surrounded by injustice, and we are also surrounded by microbes, and we must never

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:47.720
become complacent in the face of these horrors, which is my way of saying, remember to get your flu shot.

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:53.060
But we are also surrounded by love. Romantic love, friend love, family love;

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:58.460
as the poet wrote over 2000 years ago, "Love conquers all, and so we shall yield to it."

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:04.040
Thank you, to Amy and Kenny, and Sarah and Luis, and everyone else who has shared their love with us.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.060
Hank, I am going to bed. I will see you on Friday.

